From 1d1cb8697241e9e0ab20ebaf5eef28accb1ca0ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreyKatzburg <64795827+CoreyKatzburg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:46:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] capture: rtx.capture.bindInstanceMaterials, bind meshes
 whose first instance is stale

A captured mesh takes the material hash of the first instance newInstance
registers for it, and the mesh and all its instances bind only when that hash is
a captured material. The capture walks the whole instance table, which still holds
instances drawn last frame (numFramesToKeepInstances 1) and is reordered by
swap-erase. Such an instance's hash is unknown to its BLAS after the first draw
of the frame clears the material cache, so getMaterialData returns the BLAS input
material and captureMaterial stores it under that hash: the first hash never
becomes a captured material and the mesh exports unbound although its drawn
material is in Looks (con_boiler 215353: 14 meshes in each of 3 captures).

New option, default off, read when a capture starts: an instance whose own
material is captured binds it, and a mesh whose first hash is not captured binds
the captured material of its lowest-numbered instance. It only adds bindings;
with it off the export is unchanged. Decisions live in rtx_capture_binding.h so
tests/remix_source/capture_binding_test.cpp can drive them with fakes.
RtxOptions.md not regenerated (needs a game run).

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a1e070-32c4-730c-bdfc-76d09e1f79eb
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
